title ALES157 — Lotus's stereo_compress: the compressor carried into stereo, ONE LINKED GAIN from the max detector, the image held to the sample — the linked-detector law deepened into a linked-gain law
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Second rung this turn (after ALES156 stereo_gate, sent). ALES156 opened the stereo dynamics family and proved the linked-DETECTOR law. The most-reached-for member of that family is the compressor (ALES50), so it is the next crux — and it carries the gate's linking one honest step deeper into a linked-GAIN law.
think The key insight, and why the gate's law does NOT simply copy over: the gate's below-threshold attenuation is a CONSTANT factor den/num, the same for every magnitude, so gating each channel by its own magnitude already applied the same factor to both — the link there only decided WHETHER to gate. The compressor's gain factor (threshold + excess/ratio)/magnitude depends NONLINEARLY on the magnitude, so compressing each channel by its own magnitude pulls the loud channel down harder than the quiet one — different gains, image shifts. Same trap ALES129 (stereo_normalize) named for the STATIC amplitude class, now dynamic and per-sample.
think So stereo_compress computes ONE gain from the linked detector and applies it to both: key = max(|L|,|R|); if key <= thr both pass; else new_key = thr + (key-thr)*den/num (exactly ALES50's mono compress of the loud channel), then scale BOTH by the single fraction new_key/key. The peak-holding channel lands on new_key (byte-for-byte = mono compress of it), the quieter channel scaled by the identical fraction — the per-pair dynamic twin of ALES129's one-shared-gain, exactly its "the channel that held the peak lands on target, the other proportionally quieter" but recomputed each sample.
think Overflow reasoning: |sample|*new_key <= 32768*32768 fits i64; new_key <= key so the quotient <= |sample|, fits i16, sign preserved. StereoCompressError = ALES50's CompressError reused whole. Five laws witnessed first-try GREEN: linked-gain (left-always-peak master has left'=mono compress(left) {2750,-2250,500,-3000}, right scaled same fraction {687,-375,100,-1000}, independent mono compress(right)={1250,...} shown to differ), image (no expand/flip, out-of-phase equal-magnitude pair stays out of phase {2750,-2250,1750}), sub-threshold (within linked threshold identity), knob laws (unit ratio identity, higher ratio monotone, huge ratio seats loud channel at threshold 1000 / quiet at 250 proportionally), balance/atomicity/degenerate.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, values only, one multiply-then-divide per channel per sample, memoryless, a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, no red. Recorded lesson: the stereo dynamics family has TWO depths of linking — the gate links only the DECISION (constant below-threshold factor makes per-channel application already image-safe), while the compressor/limiter/expander must link the GAIN itself (a magnitude-dependent factor computed from the linked max and applied to both), because a per-channel nonlinear gain shifts the image. This is ALES129's one-shared-gain made dynamic. The limiter (ALES49) and expander (ALES60) will reuse the linked-gain shape directly; the limiter is the ratio->infinity corner already proven here as the seat-at-threshold knob law. Front doors lotus/README.md and session-logs/README.md synced in the same commit.
loom witness=ales_stereo_compress_witness result=GREEN laws=linked-gain+image+sub-threshold+knobs+balance channels=2 class=stereo-dynamics-linked-gain detector=linked-max(|L|,|R|) gain=new_key/key-shared new_key=thr+(key-thr)*den/num cases=linked-gain(left-always-peak:left'=mono-compress(left){2750,-2250,500,-3000},right-same-fraction{687,-375,100,-1000},independent-mono-right{1250,-1000,100,-1500}-differs)+image(no-expand/flip,out-of-phase-equal-mag-stays{2750,-2250,1750})+sub-threshold(within-key-identity)+knobs(unit-ratio-identity,higher-monotone,huge-seats-loud-at-1000/quiet-250)+balance/atomicity(4-refusals-untouched-balanced,count0-identity) reds=0
file lotus/stereo_compress.rye ALES157 — stereo_compress, the compressor lifted to stereo by the LINKED GAIN: key = max(|left|,|right|), new_key = thr+(key-thr)*den/num computed once, both channels scaled by the single fraction new_key/key so the peak-holder equals ALES50's mono compress and the quiet channel is scaled identically; StereoCompressError = ALES50's CompressError reused whole; the per-pair dynamic twin of ALES129's one-shared-gain.
